---
import DocsSection from '../../../layouts/DocsSection.astro';
import guides from '../../../data/app-guides.json';

const kinds = [...new Set(guides.apps.map((app) => app.kind))];
---
<DocsSection
  title="Connect an app · Azizam docs"
  heading="Connect an app"
  description="Set up an app with an Azizam protocol address and an app key."
  activeSection="connect"
>
  <p>Use the protocol your app supports. Replace <code>&lt;your gateway&gt;</code> with the HTTPS address the owner gave you.</p>

  <h2>Base paths</h2>
  <dl class="endpoint-list">
    <div><dt>OpenAI-compatible</dt><dd><code>{'https://<your gateway>/openai/v1'}</code></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Anthropic-compatible</dt><dd><code>{'https://<your gateway>/anthropic'}</code></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Ollama-compatible</dt><dd><code>{'https://<your gateway>/ollama'}</code></dd></div>
    <div><dt>MCP</dt><dd><code>{'https://<your gateway>/mcp'}</code></dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Apps, keys and trusted addresses</h2>
  <p>An App is something that connects to the gateway. A Key is the secret an app uses. The owner can add trusted addresses to an App; requests from those addresses use that App’s access plan without a key. A sent key always takes precedence.</p>
  <p>Guide steps come from each app’s documentation or source. “Unverified” marks a flow that uses third-party guidance. These guides were checked {guides.checked}.</p>

  <h2>Client guides</h2>
  {kinds.map((kind) => (
    <section class="client-guide-list">
      <h3>{kind}</h3>
      <ul>
        {guides.apps.filter((app) => app.kind === kind).map((app) => (
          <li><a href={'/docs/connect/' + app.id + '/'}>{app.name}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  ))}
</DocsSection>
